meta {
  name: User Orders Other UserId (Customer Token - Error Canary)
  type: graphql
  seq: 53
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}
  body: graphql
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

body:graphql {
  query GetUserOrdersOtherUser($userId: ID!) {
    user(id: $userId) {
      id
      orders(limit: 10, offset: 0) {
        id
      }
    }
  }
}

body:graphql:vars {
  {
    "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004"
  }
}

docs {
  Regression canary: federated User.orders queried where userId belongs to a different user, token is customer-group only.
  ACCESS_TOKEN must belong to a customer whose userId is NOT "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004".
  Expected two-layer guard:
    1. Query.user returns null (user-service BOLA guard) — orders field is never reached.
    2. If somehow user resolves, User.orders in order-service enforces assertOwnerOrOrderManagement and returns [] or throws FORBIDDEN.
  Net result: data.user = null and no orders are leaked.
  Guard under test: Query.user owner-or-management guard + order-service User.orders BOLA guard.
  Schema: apps/user-service/src/graphql/schema.ts:Query.user + apps/order-service/src/graphql/schema.ts:type.User.orders
}
